WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.135
Welcome to Nissology: the study of islands on their own terms.

00:00:05.235 --> 00:00:09.078
Over seven units we travel to six islands: a Pacific atoll,

00:00:09.078 --> 00:00:11.489
a volcano and its uplifted neighbour,

00:00:11.489 --> 00:00:15.007
a fragment of ancient continent in the South Atlantic,

00:00:15.007 --> 00:00:19.306
the most remote inhabited island on Earth, an island born in 1963,

00:00:19.306 --> 00:00:22.824
and a piece of Arabia left behind in the Indian Ocean.

00:00:23.924 --> 00:00:28.171
Each case study begins with physical geography: how the island formed,

00:00:28.171 --> 00:00:30.902
what its landforms are, and what lives there.

00:00:32.002 --> 00:00:35.715
Then we turn to history and culture: who arrived, who left,

00:00:35.715 --> 00:00:37.981
and who decides the island's future.

00:00:39.081 --> 00:00:41.456
Most of your time goes into real research.

00:00:41.456 --> 00:00:45.699
Every unit has peer-reviewed papers, annotated so you can see the argument,

00:00:45.699 --> 00:00:47.566
the evidence and the weak points.

00:00:47.566 --> 00:00:51.356
You will check their numbers, use 3D terrain models as instruments,

00:00:51.356 --> 00:00:54.127
and test yourself with quizzes after every video.
